  "id": "anticipatory-response",
  "term": "anticipatory response",
  "definition": "An anticipatory response is a stress-related bodily reaction that happens before an expected event rather than during it. In this packet, it refers to higher pre-event stress markers before a race than before routine training, suggesting the individual is reacting in advance to the upcoming challenge.",
